SIMULATION REPORT

4-Bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) using Verilog HDL

Objective
To design and simulate a 4-bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) capable of performing basic arithmetic and logical operations using Verilog HDL.

Software Used
Xilinx Vivado
Verilog HDL

Operations Implemented
Select Signal	Operation
000	Addition
001	Subtraction
010	AND
011	OR
100	NOT

Input Values Used
A = 5 (0101)
B = 3 (0011)

Simulation Procedure
The ALU module was designed using Verilog HDL.
A separate testbench was created to apply different select signal values.
Behavioral simulation was run in Xilinx Vivado.
Waveforms were observed to verify the correctness of each operation.

Waveform Analysis

The waveform shows the ALU output for different select signal values.
The inputs A and B remain constant during simulation while the select signal changes sequentially to perform different operations.
At the highlighted cursor position:

sel = 2
Operation performed = AND

Binary values:

A = 0101
B = 0011

AND operation result:

0101 AND 0011 = 0001

Therefore, the output becomes:

result = 1

The waveform correctly verifies the AND operation output.

Simulation Results
Operation	Output
Addition	8
